{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And every living thing was blotted out</b>. Their remembrance was blotted out from the earth, for they have no seed. \"And only Noah remained.\" (ונשאר רק נח לבדו) — and this is a complete refutation of the fools among our people who say that the Flood was not over all the earth."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:39.976591473Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}